            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Bisect the base with an altitude, find its length using Pythagoras, then use ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "A=\\frac{bh}{2}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "The perpendicular altitude bisects the base. Let its length be $h$.\n$$\\begin{align*}h^2+\\left(\\frac a2\\right)^2&=a^2\\\\h^2&=a^2-\\frac{a^2}{4}\\\\h^2&=\\frac{3a^2}{4}\\\\h&=\\frac{\\sqrt3a}{2}\\\\A&=\\frac{ah}{2}\\\\A&=\\frac{a}{2}\\times\\frac{\\sqrt3a}{2}\\\\A&=\\frac{\\sqrt3a^2}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 74
